{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631607-circle-of-the-crone-and-the-archtypes","id":631607,"title":"Circle of the Crone and the Archtypes...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-18T15:10:46-07:00","id":631607,"title":"Circle of the Crone and the Archtypes...","content":"One thing I noticed about the Circle of the Crone that it organizes it's members into archtypes which are apparently based on Hecate (Virgin, Maiden, Crone) and the &quot;Three faces of Adam&quot; (Fool, Hero, Prophet) which are strictly gendered based which therefore I have some serious concerns that the Circle of the Crone is problematic because of it since it apparently restricts it's members into gender roles which what if a female member of the Circle didn't want to fill in any of the Virgin, Maiden, Crone roles at all? Is the Circle really that sexist after all which it seems to adapt patriarchal gender roles that can be really rigidly restricting for it's members and what they can do?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 08-18-2015, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T15:24:05-07:00","id":631651,"title":"","content":"It actually doesn't restrict characters to the archetypes based on gender. A female member can be the Fool, the Hero, or the Father or all of them over the course of her requiem, and a male member can be the Virgin, the Maiden or the Crone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T15:28:09-07:00","id":631654,"title":"","content":"What nofather said. The Archetypes may be asociated to one gender or the other, but those members that embody them don't have to match.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T16:02:41-07:00","id":631699,"title":"","content":"Of course though what about it's sub factions or one where none of the archtypes actually exist or is it possible for Circle members to entirely ditch the archtypes all together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T16:19:30-07:00","id":631703,"title":"","content":"Yes, it says this numerous times in the introduction. The archetypes in the book are just examples, they don't represent aspects of all iterations of the covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T15:36:18-07:00","id":639528,"title":"","content":"And even if it did, you should feel free to remove it in your games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T16:38:09-07:00","id":639562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631607-circle-of-the-crone-and-the-archtypes#post631607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I noticed about the Circle of the Crone that it organizes it's members into archtypes which are apparently based on Hecate (Virgin, Maiden, Crone) and the &quot;Three faces of Adam&quot; (Fool, Hero, Prophet) which are strictly gendered based which therefore I have some serious concerns that the Circle of the Crone is problematic because of it since it apparently restricts it's members into gender roles which what if a female member of the Circle didn't want to fill in any of the Virgin, Maiden, Crone roles at all? Is the Circle really that sexist after all which it seems to adapt patriarchal gender roles that can be really rigidly restricting for it's members and what they can do?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, it actually organizes them into four each - virgin, maiden, crone, and scarlet woman, for instance. That fourth is for the outlier group. And, no, you don't HAVE to necessarily fit into those neat categories - there are some cases of transgender women vamps fitting into the female roles. However, its not unusual for some to try and be forced into what they consider more appropriate roles.<br /> <br /> When all is said and done, there IS more than a bit of sexism in the Circle. In some ways, the Lance is more progressive than the CotC, as its much more gender-blind when it comes to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 08-25-2015, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T17:47:13-07:00","id":639658,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say that it is a bit more sexist, but that it reveals sexism easier. The Lancea is gender-blind, the Circle is gender-centered, but both could be progressive or sexist in extremes.<br /> <br /> What happens is that the Circle makes gender a constant theme, while the Lancea does not. So one makes personal opinions more easy to come to the fore, and prejudice to be more blatant by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T19:06:03-07:00","id":639702,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that the title of Prince is uni-sexual. I suppose there are vampires who prefer to be called Princess, but I've yet to see an example of it. So I don't see why just because a role is named after a certain gender means you have to be that gender.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T07:19:10-07:00","id":640154,"title":"","content":"The Circle is more likely to call certain pairings &quot;unnatural&quot; than the Lance. For instance, in the covenant book, it actually flat out said the Lance was more progressive about same-sex matches than the Circle (if I recall correctly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T08:26:12-07:00","id":640206,"title":"","content":"Eh, if you want to have a character whose concept boils down to 'Transgender Maiden of the [insert provocative Crone cult name]', more power to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T23:03:02-07:00","id":641163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631607-circle-of-the-crone-and-the-archtypes?p=640154#post640154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Circle is more likely to call certain pairings &quot;unnatural&quot; than the Lance. For instance, in the covenant book, it actually flat out said the Lance was more progressive about same-sex matches than the Circle (if I recall correctly).</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I could understand, the Lance is also more prone to remove the notion of sex from any pairing. And that's very in-tune with Christian moral. &quot;Friendship&quot; among same-sex people is seen as good, sex itself is what is reviled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T04:45:04-07:00","id":641395,"title":"","content":"In simple terms, both covenants consider vampires to be ideally asexual beings. The Circle has roles based on the concept of gender, but it would be up to a specific cult to determine an individual's eligibility to take up a role. A female cult member might take a male philosophical role as readily as one of the female roles. The Circle even has marriage, but there are no gender roles in that. Vampires are not supposed to procreate in the mortal sense. They don't raise children. They only take actual gender roles when dealing with mortals. Within the covenant, socially they would be androgynous. Actual gender would only be important for whatever rituals they choose to enact. They are vampires and won't be held down by concepts that apply to mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T05:50:18-07:00","id":641426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631607-circle-of-the-crone-and-the-archtypes?p=641395#post641395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In simple terms, both covenants consider vampires to be ideally asexual beings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an interesting point. And the Monachal creed, the most widely followed creed of the Lancea et Sanctum, actually forbids vampires from having romantic relationships with other vampires.<br /> <br /> So it's possible they're not as much open-minded regarding sexuality as viewing vampires as another sex entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T14:24:03-07:00","id":642091,"title":"","content":"Either Covenant can be as sexist as you need it to be for your story. They're collections of individuals with their own prejudiced views of doctrine. A stony Lancea patriarch condemning the abominable sodomy of homosexual vampires is just as likely as one who ordains the Adelphopoiesis of two of his brothers-in-faith. A scowling Crone matriarch exiling a transgender vampire from her Amazonian circle is just as likely as one who welcomes that same vampire as their new Maiden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T04:19:42-07:00","id":642829,"title":"","content":"That would be the other side of things, the &quot;human&quot; element, so the local chapter can fall anywhere on the spectrum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T12:33:22-07:00","id":648257,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>plays a game with themes of sexual transgression, mental violation, physical violation, human sacrifice, and cannibalism</li> <li>worries about &quot;problematic gender roles&quot;</li> </ul>Not to be a jerk, but this isn't Bunnies and Burrows. If the game makes you uncomfortable, then don't play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T13:04:41-07:00","id":648285,"title":"","content":"The game can have any elements in it that you want and can do without any you or your particular group finds uncomfortable. If human sacrifice or canibalism, to draw two from your list, is triggery for any of the participants the solution is not &quot;not playing the game&quot; is playing without those elements.<br /> <br /> Your post has exactly zero constructive advice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T05:55:16-07:00","id":648771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631607-circle-of-the-crone-and-the-archtypes?p=640154#post640154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Circle is more likely to call certain pairings &quot;unnatural&quot; than the Lance. For instance, in the covenant book, it actually flat out said the Lance was more progressive about same-sex matches than the Circle (if I recall correctly).</div> </div> </div> </div>Transgenderism pops up more in non christian context. Legends of Attis castrating himself for example.<br /> Shamanistic rituals where someone who is sick has their identity changed temporarly by the shamen to confuse the disease spirits.<br /> <br /> As far as the LS is concerned PAul had all kinds of issues any kind of sex.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T10:35:25-07:00","id":649103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631607-circle-of-the-crone-and-the-archtypes?p=648771#post648771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transgenderism pops up more in non christian context. Legends of Attis castrating himself for example.<br /> Shamanistic rituals where someone who is sick has their identity changed temporarly by the shamen to confuse the disease spirits.<br /> <br /> As far as the LS is concerned Paul had all kinds of issues any kind of sex.</div> </div> </div> </div> Still doesn't change that the CotC book specifically said that they found some things unnatural. Take from it what you will. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T18:32:52-07:00","id":651961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631607-circle-of-the-crone-and-the-archtypes?p=649103#post649103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Still doesn't change that the CotC book specifically said that they found some things unnatural. Take from it what you will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Unnatural, really? Coming from a cult that practices blood magic and worships ancient, pagan deities who demanded some really fucked up rituals from their worshipers? Yeah, gender is the last thing they have any right to be concerned about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T20:22:51-07:00","id":652049,"title":"","content":"Before this thread becomes the one they link to when someone wants to call the entire Circle of the Crone a bunch of of homophobes, lets get a quote in here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Circle of the Crone p87</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">'That said, there is a segment of the Circle, that cares about homosexuality. These Acolytes don\u2019t care about it as a lifestyle choice (since they don\u2019t have lives) but rather as a philosophical and mystical issue. Among those with an opinion, the split is almost perfectly even between those who tolerate and even celebrate alternative sexuality, and those who despise and condemn it.<br /> <br /> The intolerant faction adheres to what they call \u201cthe principle of Natural Life.\u201d They believe in an ordered cosmos in which everything has a place and a purpose. Transgressing that order is not just wrong, it\u2019s dangerous. Similar to fundamentalist Christianity and Islam, Natural Life Acolytes argue that living men have penises so they can impregnate living women, full stop. Unlike those mortal religions, Natural Life Acolytes cite direct experience of the supernatural as proof of cosmic order. Creation is good, and fertility is to be praised. Stagnant lustful rutting is, at best, a waste and a symptom of a greater malaise. At worst, it\u2019s an affront to nature itself (although only the most fanatical fraction of the faction considers the damage anything but minor).<br /> <br /> On the other side of the fence sit the Transgressionists, who think it\u2019s pretty rich that a blood-drinking animate corpse would dare lecture anyone about \u201cLife\u201d or what\u2019s \u201cNatural.\u201d Sure, standard vanilla man-woman sex creates babies and serves that function in the normal course of things.'</div> </div> </div> </div>The Circle as a whole does not view homosexuality as unnatural, but there is a faction that does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-05-2015, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T19:32:19-07:00","id":653400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631607-circle-of-the-crone-and-the-archtypes?p=651961#post651961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unnatural, really? Coming from a cult that practices blood magic and worships ancient, pagan deities who demanded some really fucked up rituals from their worshipers? Yeah, gender is the last thing they have any right to be concerned about.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you believe that blood magic and the pagan deities are natural there is no logical inconsistencies. The idea of vampires and what they do being a natural part of reality was a pretty big theme in 1st ed. I can absolutely see how a believer of that could also believe subverting 'natural born/given gender' is unnatural.<br /> <br /> I'd disagree, and much prefer the idea of transgressive members of the circle, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}